{"duration_api_ms":97002,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"61db9a1d-14b7-4a4a-ba7d-522a6b6d4cd9","total_cost_usd":0.48870820000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":80653,"cache_read_input_tokens":83236,"output_tokens":9657,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2085},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":80653,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3774,"cache_read_input_tokens":78914,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6061},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":52771,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.052871,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":9657,"cacheReadInputTokens":83236,"cacheCreationInputTokens":80653,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.43583720000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2085,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"node2 (lan-a) -> node3 (lan-b) connections observed by node3 as arriving from a chosen address on node1, not node2's own address\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline TCP test (cmd-0c9b62102bf8422d, node3 conns log cmd-ea06e0295fae4802) showed node3 seeing the real node2 address (10.60.10.2) before the SNAT rule existed. After the directional SNAT rule (interface opt2, source_net opt1, target 10.60.20.1) was installed and confirmed active in pf (cmd-fdd0ee6b9ffd42fe: 'nat on vtnet2 inet from (vtnet1:network) to any -> 10.60.20.1'), a fresh connection (cmd-ace9b669045e464f) and node3's connection log (cmd-ea06e0295fae4802) showed the source as 10.60.20.1 -- node1's chosen lan-b address. This was re-verified after each of the three node restarts (cmd-9e0a3af2a5834e19, cmd-4427d6ec3c234cd3, cmd-4a91711312c442c3), consistently showing 10.60.20.1 as the observed source.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0c9b62102bf8422d\",\"cmd-ea06e0295fae4802\",\"cmd-fdd0ee6b9ffd42fe\",\"cmd-ace9b669045e464f\",\"cmd-9e0a3af2a5834e19\",\"cmd-4427d6ec3c234cd3\",\"cmd-4a91711312c442c3\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Connections in the reverse direction (node3 lan-b -> node2 lan-a) keep their original source address (no NAT applied)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline reverse connection (cmd-668e9640cd454ed0) showed node2 observing node3's real address (10.60.20.2). After the SNAT rule for the opposite direction (lan-a->lan-b only) was installed, the reverse-direction test (cmd-8e61d06b46784afe) and node2's connection log (cmd-6c89b8d55ac945ae) continued to show the unmodified source 10.60.20.2, confirming asymmetric behavior. Re-verified after each restart (cmd-f0652c983d3c43b8, cmd-6780975e1b1a4040, cmd-b27a8cdd1abc4751), always showing 10.60.20.2 unchanged.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-668e9640cd454ed0\",\"cmd-8e61d06b46784afe\",\"cmd-6c89b8d55ac945ae\",\"cmd-f0652c983d3c43b8\",\"cmd-6780975e1b1a4040\",\"cmd-b27a8cdd1abc4751\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"SNAT rule correctly implemented as outbound source translation (not accidentally a port-forward/DNAT) and persisted in node1 configuration\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An initial rule was mistakenly placed under the legacy <nat><rule> section (cmd-b2e6ebc3cab6458f), which pfctl showed materialized as an 'rdr' (destination NAT/port-forward) rule rather than SNAT (cmd-6d06db05a52e484a). The executor detected this, removed the erroneous rule, and added a proper rule under OPNsense/Firewall/Filter/snatrules (cmd-8b187ff0808c4df4), after which pfctl -s nat showed the correct outbound SNAT line 'nat on vtnet2 inet from (vtnet1:network) to any -> 10.60.20.1' (cmd-fdd0ee6b9ffd42fe). Config persistence was confirmed via config.xml inspection showing opt1/opt2 interfaces, hybrid NAT mode, and 1 snatrules entry (cmd-3899f7587d104680), and this rule was shown to auto-restore after node1's own reboot (cmd-0fcd30a2dec04493).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b2e6ebc3cab6458f\",\"cmd-6d06db05a52e484a\",\"cmd-8b187ff0808c4df4\",\"cmd-fdd0ee6b9ffd42fe\",\"cmd-3899f7587d104680\",\"cmd-0fcd30a2dec04493\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed for all three managed nodes with pre-restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, and full recovery of NAT/data-plane behavior\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For node2: boot_id captured before (cmd-fddbdf7f26c94295: 9bdcc129...) and after reboot (cmd-36f1e211a3d4442a: c6fe83df...), matching the fixed after_executor snapshot; interface/route/firewalld state and NAT test behavior re-verified post-reboot (cmd-c1485032b3ff489c, cmd-9e0a3af2a5834e19). For node3: boot_id before (cmd-ae490fdce83c43ee: f54d7366...) and after (cmd-76a8c81aac43409e: c182563a...), matching fixed snapshot; recovery verified (cmd-ec226773369c45ab, cmd-4427d6ec3c234cd3). For node1 (FreeBSD): kern.boottime before (cmd-3899f7587d104680: 16:24:16) and after (cmd-bba0bc428ac84125: 16:30:25), matching the fixed after_executor snapshot value; full pf/interface/NAT rule auto-recovery and end-to-end NAT behavior reconfirmed post-reboot (cmd-0fcd30a2dec04493, cmd-4a91711312c442c3, cmd-b27a8cdd1abc4751). All three nodes show the required pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, distinct post-restart boot identity, and recovered service/data/NAT state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fddbdf7f26c94295\",\"cmd-36f1e211a3d4442a\",\"cmd-c1485032b3ff489c\",\"cmd-9e0a3af2a5834e19\",\"cmd-ae490fdce83c43ee\",\"cmd-76a8c81aac43409e\",\"cmd-ec226773369c45ab\",\"cmd-4427d6ec3c234cd3\",\"cmd-3899f7587d104680\",\"cmd-bba0bc428ac84125\",\"cmd-0fcd30a2dec04493\",\"cmd-4a91711312c442c3\",\"cmd-b27a8cdd1abc4751\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.6,\"summary\":\"Most executor mutations were necessary and correctly scoped: adding opt1/opt2 interfaces, filter pass rules, and the directional SNAT rule on node1; and configuring eth1 static IPs/routes on node2/node3 as a required prerequisite for testing cross-lan connectivity. One troubleshooting mistake occurred: cmd-b2e6ebc3cab6458f placed an outbound-NAT rule under the legacy <nat><rule> section, which pf revealed to be a DNAT/port-forward rather than SNAT (cmd-6d06db05a52e484a); this was corrected by removing the rule and adding a proper snatrules entry in cmd-8b187ff0808c4df4 -- a bounded, fully-reverted misstep with no lasting residue, but it should still be counted as an unnecessary mutation per policy. More significant residue: test echo-server listeners left permanently running after task completion on node2 (10.60.10.2:5001, python3 pid 849, cmd-dfc009afc6bb4035) and node3 (10.60.20.2:5000, python3 pid 836, cmd-e7fec28f91ff41ab), plus permanent firewalld port openings for 5000/tcp and 5001/tcp (cmd-4e8a98dc651644ec, cmd-65963d0fc6094e56, cmd-a50f4fa984ee4734, cmd-7eafb25488d14733) that remain in the after_executor listening-sockets snapshot -- these are verification artifacts, not part of the deliverable, and were not cleaned up, leaving open listening services and firewall exposure on both AlmaLinux nodes. Backup copies of config.xml (.bak1-.bak4) were also left on node1 without cleanup, though this is low-risk residue.\",\"evidence_ids\"
